course: dictionary
lesson: 16104
title: Wedged: stuck tight
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Wedged means stuck tightly in a narrow space, so it cannot easily move. «The ball was wedged between two rocks.» The ball is stuck in a tight gap and will not roll out. The clue is the narrow space.
explain: To wedge something means to push it tightly into a space, or to hold something open or shut with a wedge. «Ella wedged the door open with a stone.» Ella pushed the stone under the door so it could not swing shut. Ask yourself: what is stopping something from moving?
explain: Wedged often appears with words like «wedged in», «wedged between», «wedged open» and «wedged shut». «Tom was wedged between two big boys on the crowded bus.» Between tells you where Tom was, and wedged tells you he was squeezed in tightly with no room to spare.
fact: Wedged means stuck tightly in a narrow space.
fact: To wedge something means to push it tightly into a space, or to hold something open or shut.
fact: A wedge is a simple machine, like an axe blade or a doorstop, that pushes things apart or holds them in place.
fact: «Wedged open» means held open by something pushed into the gap, like a doorstop.
fact: Wedged is the past form of the verb «wedge»: wedge, wedges, wedged, wedging.
exercise: «The ball was wedged in the gap between the fence posts.» What does wedged mean here? | *Stuck tightly in a narrow space | Lost for ever in the long grass | Bouncing high in the air | Rolling quickly down the hill
exercise: «Ella wedged the door open with a stone.» What did Ella do? | She knocked the door down | *She pushed a stone under the door to hold it open | She locked the door shut with a key | She painted the door red
exercise: «The cat was wedged between two cushions on the sofa.» Find and copy the word that shows the cat was stuck tightly. | cat | sofa | cushions | *wedged
test: «Tom was wedged between two big boys on the crowded bus.» Where was Tom? | Asleep in the driver's seat | *Squeezed tightly between two boys | Standing outside the bus in the rain | Sitting alone at the front of the bus
test: A wedge is a simple machine. What job does a wedge do? | It makes sounds louder | It makes things melt | It lights up a dark room | *It pushes things apart or holds them in place
exam: Which sentence uses wedged to mean pushed tightly into a space? | She wedged the yellow paint. | The sky was wedged blue. | The wedged dog ran away. | *«He wedged the box under the bed to stop it wobbling.»
